details:
When i want make World Clock, some functions can used to adjust time.
Example:
DateTime utc = DateTime.UtcNow;
DateTime now = utc.ToLocalTime();
TimeZoneInfo zone = TimeZoneInfo.FindSystemTimeZoneById(timeZoneString);
DateTime zoneTime = TimeZoneInfo.ConvertTime(utc, zone);

Class is written here: https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.timezoneinfo?view=net-6.0

Problem: you need know the correct timezone names for convert time. For that, there is help from it:
https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.timezoneinfo.getsystemtimezones?view=net-6.0

Yes, that is with: ReadOnlyCollection<TimeZoneInfo> timeZones = TimeZoneInfo.GetSystemTimeZones();

But i got message it's not added to Udon. Huh?

Why have you added other functions but NOT GetSystemTimeZones()? That makes the function TimeZoneInfo partially useless because you don't know exact names. I am forced to load text file with zone names (as TextAsset) as help.

Please make it fully complete class, not half way. There is no security risk, it's just read-only information.
This will save troubles for making World Clock scripts, especially around New Year (and other special date events).
I managed get it work with external text file, but this is just not great. Lost hours to figure out and it was just missing function, not fully complete class.

Thank you.
